NNAAMMEE
     bbiiffff — be notified if mail arrives and who it is from

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     bbiiffff [nn | yy]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     bbiiffff informs the system whether you want to be notified when mail arrives
     during the current terminal session.

     The options are as follows:

     nn       Disables notification.

     yy       Enables notification.

     When mail notification is enabled, the header and first few lines of the
     message will be printed on your screen whenever mail arrives.  A “biff y”
     command is often included in the file _._l_o_g_i_n or _._p_r_o_f_i_l_e to be executed
     at each login.

     bbiiffff operates asynchronously.  For synchronous notification use the MAIL
     variable of sh(1) or the mail variable of csh(1).

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The bbiiffff utility exits with one of the following values:

     0       Notification was enabled at the time of invocation.

     1       Notification was disabled at the time of invocation.

     >1      An error occurred.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     csh(1), mail(1), sh(1), comsat(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The bbiiffff command appeared in 4.0BSD.  "Biff" was Heidi Stettner's dog.
     He died in August 1993, at 15.

